<article class="env-lemma" id="0E1S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E1S">Lemma <span data-tag="0E1S">15.6.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/08KH" data-tag="08KH">15.6.1</a> if $B \to A$ is integral, then $B' \to A'$ is integral. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $a' \in A'$ with image $a \in A$. Let $x^ d + b_1 x^{d - 1} + \ldots + b_ d$ be a monical polynomial with coefficients in $B$ satisfied by $a$. Choose $b'_ i \in B'$ mapping to $b_ i \in B$ (possible). Then $(a')^ d + b'_1 (a')^{d - 1} + \ldots + b'_ d$ is in the kernel of $A' \to A$. Since $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(B' \to B) = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(A' \to A)$ we can modify our choice of $b'_ d$ to get $(a')^ d + b'_1 (a')^{d - 1} + \ldots + b'_ d = 0$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>